# TypeScript Standards

## General

- Prefer `async/await` over raw Promises.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow, or proper types from `@/lib/supabase/types` and `@/lib/api`.
- Use typed errors: `AuthError`, `ValidationError` from `@/lib/api/validation` where applicable.

## Error Handling

```typescript
// BAD - swallow errors
try {
  await doSomething();
} catch (e) {}

// GOOD - log and rethrow or return apiError
try {
  await doSomething();
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Context:", error);
  return apiError("User-friendly message", 500);
}
```

## Supabase

- Use `createApiClient()` or `createAdminClient()` from `@/lib/api`.
- Type results from Supabase with `Database["public"]["Tables"]["table_name"]` when needed; avoid untyped `.select("*")` in new code when you need specific columns.
